This product is an independent implementation of an interface that was
recovered by observing the behaviour of a device driver on the author's own
hardware. It contains no NVIDIA source code, no NVIDIA binary, no firmware and
no dumped memory.

Derivative interface documentation:
  nvidia-smi, without nvidia-smi — reverse-engineering notes
  https://github.com/zagg/nvidia-smi-clone-RE  (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 zagg)
  Files relied upon: include/nvrm.h, include/rusd.h, src/nvrm.c, src/fields.c,
  docs/REVERSE_ENGINEERING.md, docs/FINDINGS.md.

Structures and constants that NVIDIA ships under MIT with its open kernel module
(class/cl00de.h, ctrl/ctrl2080/*.h, nvos.h, nvstatuscodes.h) are used as the
reference for field layouts; only the facts they state are reproduced here.

